Subject: [PATCH 03/12] marianos-azure-headless 1.10.0rc6 (tests only):
 validate-export reads a run's stored pages one at a time and checks every
 record's capture (OR-20)

validate-export of run F2 (575 stored listing pages) was killed for lack of memory on the operator's 3.8 GiB
VM: 1.10.0rc5 reads every stored page, then indexes every embedded product object at once. These tests state
the bounded behaviour: each page read and indexed before the next, distinct price statements kept once, every
exported record's capture (the stored page the published supporting log names) present with its recorded
SHA-256, missing and altered pages named per record and rejected, and each mismatch named with both values
and its source. Expected to fail on 1.10.0rc5 (5 tests: 3 integration, 2 unit); the control passes on both.
---
